{
  "_doc": "Single source of truth for the studio's motion grammar. The names and control points follow motion.dev (framer-motion's named easings) so any recipe copied from https://motion.dev/docs can be typed straight into engine K (templates/render/lib/motion.js) or engine P (templates/procedural-reels/motion.py). tests/test_motion.py fails if either engine drifts from this file. `formulas` are the classic Penner equations (as implemented by the MIT 'easing-functions' package) for the shapes a cubic-bezier cannot express: elastic, bounce, and the exact quad/cubic/quart/quint/sine/expo families. They deliberately use names that do not collide with the bezier vocabulary.",
